I'm mapping the rest of the events: S3 ListBuckets and GetObject, and CloudWatch Logs DescribeLogGroups. Since s3:GetObject ideally needs a specific bucket/object ARN but I don't have bucket names from the events, I'll note that limitation and use a wildcard with a caveat, grouping the account-level actions that inherently require resource "*" separately from the scoped ones.

"}]}

{"id": "05f92ad5-1aaf-4673-a19e-130494968f10", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Based on exactly those five API calls, here's the least-privilege policy — no `*` beyond what each action structurally requires:

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "LambdaInventoryRead",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "lambda:ListFunctions",
        "lambda:GetFunction"
      ],
      "Resource": "*"
    },
    {
      "Sid": "S3InventoryRead",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:ListAllMyBuckets",
      "Resource": "*"
    },
    {
      "Sid": "S3ObjectRead",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "[redacted ARN]"
    },
    {
      "Sid": "LogsInventoryRead",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "logs:DescribeLogGroups",
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}
```

Notes on scoping:
- `lambda:ListFunctions`, `s3:ListAllMyBuckets`, and `logs:DescribeLogGroups` are account/region-level list actions in IAM — they don't support resource-level restriction, so `"Resource": "*"` is the tightest this can go per AWS's own action definitions.
